1324:#  DATED, NAMED DEBT -- not a count and not a silent allowlist.  gate_offline.sh MEASURED that
1325:#  a COUNT pin actively obstructs the shrink it claims to want ("6, shrinking not growing" went
1326:#  RED at 5).  A date expires; shrinking is green by construction.
1327:#
1328:#  2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in
1329:#  gate_offline.sh's SM_EXEMPT, so #442's two debts fall due together.  IT IS A PROPOSAL: the
1330:#  owner set the SM dates and set them TIGHTER than the ones proposed, and a deadline nobody
1331:#  chose is a deadline nobody owns.
1332:#
1333:#  These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and
1334:#  exits nonzero on failure.  What each needs is a gate that owns it, its rig preconditions,
1335:#  and ONE clean gate run proving it green before it ships.  That last part is why they are
1336:#  exempted here rather than wired here: gate_hygiene's own comments record FOUR probes that
1337:#  shipped latently RED because the commit that added them never fired the gate.
1338:EXEMPT = {
1339:    #  pit8253_latch_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- it is now wired into
1340:    #  gate_arm.sh beside footbridge_sites_probe.py, which is the home gate_hygiene.sh's own
1341:    #  bump note named for it ("wants an operator who can run that gate").  The entry is
1342:    #  DELETED rather than dated forward, in the SAME edit that added the wiring, because a
1343:    #  wired probe that keeps an exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it.
1344:    #  Seven exemptions remain.
1345:    #  sh4_bsc_width_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- wired into
1346:    #  gate_sh_rounding.sh, whose `-E landisk` machine it already used.  Deleted in the
1347:    #  SAME edit as the wiring, because a wired probe that keeps an exemption is a
1348:    #  STALE EXEMPTION.  Six exemptions remain.
