1429:#  A python interpreter token.  Bare python/python3, or the $PY-style indirections other
1430:#  harnesses in this tree use.  Anchored so python3.12 and mypython do not match.
1431:#  *** THE TRAILING BOUNDARY IS LOAD-BEARING AND THE FIRST VERSION LACKED IT. ***  A
1432:#  flagship review MEASURED that `"$PYLINT" probe.py` scored as WIRING: the alternation
1433:#  had no boundary after the group, so ANY $PY-prefixed variable read as an interpreter
1434:#  and a linter invocation would have marked a probe wired.  That is the FALSE ACCEPT
1435:#  direction -- the one that silently stops demanding a gate.  Latent rather than live:
1436:#  no such variable exists in the battery today.  `$PYTHON` and `$PY` still match;
1437:#  `$PYLINT` and `$PYTEST` no longer do.
1438:INTERP_RE = re.compile(
1439:    r'"?\$\{?(?:PY|PY3|PYTHON|PYTHON3)\}?"?(?![A-Za-z0-9_])'
1440:    r'|(?<![\w./-])python3?(?![\w.-])'
1441:)
1442:
1443:#  COMMAND POSITION -- the whole defence against "a mention counts as wiring".  Everything
1444:#  before the interpreter must be shell scaffolding: leading space, an assignment opening a
1445:#  command substitution (out=$( ), control keywords, and environment-variable prefixes.
1446:#
1447:#  THE LINE THIS WAS BUILT AGAINST IS REAL AND LIVE, not invented:
1448:#      gate_hygiene.sh:331   note "diag_div_sweep.py or python3 missing -- class ratchet NOT run"
1449:#  It carries a probe basename AND the token python3 on one non-comment line, and it is a
1450:#  message saying the probe DID NOT RUN.  A two-sided "name near python" regex scores it as
1451:#  execution.  Here the interpreter's prefix is `note "diag_div_sweep.py or `, which is not
1452:#  scaffolding, so the line is rejected.
1453:CMDPOS_RE = re.compile(
1454:    r"""^\s*
1455:        (?: [A-Za-z_]\w* = (?:\$\()? \s* )?
1456:        (?: (?: if | then | else | elif | while | until | do | ! | \$\( | \( ) \s* )*
1457:        (?: [A-Za-z_]\w* = (?: "[^"]*" | '[^']*' | \S* ) \s+ )*
1458:        $""",
1459:    re.X,
1460:)
1461:
1462:VAR_RE = re.compile(r"^\$\{?([A-Za-z_]\w*)\}?$")
1463:ASSIGN_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*([A-Za-z_]\w*)=(\S+)")
