Thus premise 3 is **corrected to eight of 25 from notes, with at least nine supported by inspected repository evidence**. The IRQ-stub rationale is present verbatim. The claim that this happens *faster* than exemptions retire requires historical measurements; this snapshot does not establish that rate.

My latest read-only checker run returned exit 0 and:

`PROBEWIRING_PASS 59/65 detectors run by a gate, 6 dated-exempt, 25 witnesses correctly ungated`

That directly demonstrates the classification problem.

For Q2, the proposed single rule is:

> **For probe entries added or changed after CUTOFF = 2026-09-09, require either CLASS_DETECTOR with a derived gate invocation, a valid unexpired EXEMPT naming the round owing its detector wiring, or an ungated CLASS_WITNESS explicitly declaring “post-fix green NEVER measured” and a pre-fix-symptom oracle; report unchanged on/before-cutoff violations as archived debt.**

I would use **structured MANIFEST fields**, covering the declaration date, post-fix-green status, oracle polarity, and evidence reference. The note remains readable explanation. The round must migrate existing declarations by inspecting their notes and cited evidence.

The three passing dispositions are exact:

1. **Wired detector:** `CLASS_DETECTOR`, repaired-property oracle, and an invocation derived from the battery’s scripts. A claimed gate name in the note does not suffice.
2. **Deferred detector:** a valid calendar expiry date, not yet expired, and an explicit owing-round ID. To satisfy Q3’s “same entry” control, a measured-green entry may temporarily retain `CLASS_WITNESS`, but must render as **exempt detector debt**. This requires narrowly changing today’s orphan-exemption rejection; true symptom witnesses must remain ineligible.
3. **True witness:** `CLASS_WITNESS`, no gate invocation, an explicit “post-fix green NEVER measured” declaration, and a declaration that its assertions expect the pre-fix symptom and would reject the repair. An unmeasured repaired-property probe cannot use this route.

The checker must enumerate every relevant entry and require the fields, rather than select entries whose prose happens to match a regex. Missing or unknown live declarations fail explicitly. Its summary must account for every entry as enforced or archived; zero enforced entries must visibly mean “all archived.”

Because MANIFEST currently has no entry dates, cutoff migration also needs a frozen inventory of the existing entry/probe versions. Only those unchanged versions qualify for archival treatment; a new entry cannot obtain grandfathering by supplying an old date. Missing dates outside that inventory are new, following the bugfile precedent.

This cannot prove that a human’s `NEVER` declaration is truthful. It does prevent an omitted marker or unfamiliar wording from silently removing an entry from consideration.

For Q3, these are **proposed control outputs**, not measurements performed during this review. Use an otherwise clean fixture, with the checker’s clock fixed at 2026-09-10.

| Control | Required result | Distinguishing output |
|---|---|---|
| **C1:** `synthetic_postfix_green_probe.py`, declared witness, declaration dated 2026-09-10, measured-green status, no invocation or exemption | Exit **1** | `WITNESSCLASS_FAIL synthetic_postfix_green_probe.py post_fix=MEASURED_GREEN gate=NONE exempt=NONE`, followed by `PROBEWIRING_FAIL` |
| **C2:** Identical entry, plus an exemption through 2026-09-20 naming `wiringcliff` | Exit **0** | `WITNESSCLASS_EXEMPT synthetic_postfix_green_probe.py until=2026-09-20 round=wiringcliff probe=NOT_RUN`, followed by `PROBEWIRING_PASS` |
| **C3:** Same contradiction genuinely present in the pre-cutoff fixture inventory, dated 2026-09-08 | Exit **0**, debt reported | `WITNESSCLASS_ARCHIVED synthetic_postfix_green_probe.py cutoff=2026-09-09 probe=NOT_RUN`, with `archived_class_debt=1` in the summary |

The selftest must require **all three named cases to execute**, assert both exit status and the case-specific diagnostic, and print `WITNESSCLASS_SELFTEST_PASS executed=3/3` only afterward. A missing case must produce `WITNESSCLASS_SELFTEST_FAIL`, preserving the expected denominator. Checking only for `PROBEWIRING_PASS` would make C2 indistinguishable from a checker that never examined the entry.

For Q4, **no unchanged existing entry incurs a new day-one failure under that cutoff**. The nine evidenced cases become reported migration work. Enforcing them immediately would contradict the proposed archival treatment.

These are their cheapest candidate homes, based on existing interfaces and gate structure:

| Entry | Candidate gate section and material cost |
|---|---|
| `alpha_harness_probe.py` | `gate_asan_sweep.sh`: a normal-binary section following the `sgi_eaddr_probe.py` pattern; independent log and result checks. |
| `lca_confwidth_probe.py` | Same normal-binary section pattern; parse and require its complete result. |
| `lca_irqstub_probe.py` | Same pattern; require its completion token and passing result. Its process exit status alone does not establish success. |
| `alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py` | Same pattern; independent result and emitted-row checks. |
| `alpha_swpctx_v0_probe.py` | Same pattern; require `SWPCTXV0_DONE` and a fully passing result, because the script prints failures without setting a failing exit status. |
| `artifacts/alphatbinegsel/witness_agy_20260908/alphatbi_probe.asrun.py` | Same pattern, invoking the exact nested path; require its completion/result contract. |
| `sgi_mte_fill_probe.py` | `gate_arm.sh`: the existing SGI `sgi_re_randompixel_probe.py` section has the closest shape—normal binary, individual log, completion and row checks. This compounds the already-recorded device-gate split debt. |
| `artifacts/shortread/round_20260827/shortread_witness.py` | `gate_sh_rounding.sh`: reuse its normal binary and landisk kernel; supply a dedicated work directory. The script already creates its fixture. Require its PASS token and five emitted rows; exit status alone is insufficient. |
| `artifacts/wdcnoirq/witness_20260827/wdcnoirq_rung3_probe.py` | `gate_sh_rounding.sh`: the `wdc_flood_probe.py` section already uses the matching binary/kernel/scratch-disk shape. Require control success and the complete result; redirect its transcript output before regular use so archived evidence is not overwritten. |

Placement is consequential:

- **ASan gate:** put the independent normal-binary sections **after `gate_begin` at line 97 and before the ASan-only `gate_skip` at line 99**. The existing eaddr invocation at line 551 is itself downstream of that exit. [ASan preflight](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_asan_sweep.sh:97), [normal-binary precedent](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_asan_sweep.sh:538)
- **ARM gate:** put an independent SGI section after the shared binary/Python preflight at lines 81–82 and before ARM-stub creation, whose failure exits at line 90. Appending it below later ARM probe exits makes its execution depend on unrelated sections. [ARM preflight](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_arm.sh:75), [SGI section pattern](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_arm.sh:1282)
- **SH gate:** put the new independent sections after the common preflight at lines 34–36 and before the rounding probe and its line-47 exit. Give WDCNOIRQ its own disk preflight; shortread must remain reachable without the unrelated scratch-disk requirement that currently exits at line 1385. [SH preflight](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh:30), [WDC section pattern](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh:1383)

The shortread fixture cost is smaller than its manifest explanation suggests: its `main()` constructs the fixture itself. WDCNOIRQ needs output-location work because it writes a transcript alongside its script. [Shortread fixture creation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shortread/round_20260827/shortread_witness.py:219), [WDCNOIRQ transcript destination](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/wdcnoirq/witness_20260827/wdcnoirq_rung3_probe.py:398)

A maintainer would have concrete reasons to switch the rule off if it retro-failed the archive, treated `PENDING` or green control rows as whole-probe success, demanded routine execution of symptom-inverting witnesses, or forced gates to depend on unavailable unrelated rigs. Requiring immediate gate green against `build/gxemul` when the measured fix exists only in a candidate build would cause the same problem. Those cases need visible dated debt.

The wiring estimates above are structural, without runtime measurements. Each home still owes a clean run, result-parser validation, and proof that its section remains reachable when unrelated prerequisites are missing.

Evidence basis: I read the specified working tree’s manifest, class branches, EXEMPT handling, gate derivation, cutoff precedent, relevant shell sections, probe interfaces, and the cited preserved results. I ran text searches, AST census checks, and the existing read-only wiring checker. I did not run emulator probes or the proposed controls. The panel’s voting history and the precise authorship/date of its classification decision remain packet claims; the IRQ-stub rationale itself is verified in the file.
